Z||000002||Formula||10-10-2000||09:54 PM||||it reads volts not amps so ........ maybe it drops when something such as a radiator comes on.  but its not a good thing if it actually making 18 volts instead of 12-14, next youll need an ac volt meter||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-10-2000||11:13 PM||||get a real volt meter and measure the voltage across the battery with the car running and stopped. Don't ever trust a dash volt meter to be acurate.<P>If you don't have or can get a volt meter (They are cheap at Wall Mart.) take it to autozone pep boys or most other parts stores. most of tehm will stick the machine on and check the whole charging system for free.||||reg||1
Z||000004||007DOUG||10-11-2000||11:12 PM||||Several of my fieros have done that, ummm......for as long as I can remember.<P>I have a plug-in voltage meter that ogre spoke of. It'll read as high as 18.7 volts at times, never a problem though.||||reg||1
